Agent folders for herdr-app
https://github.com/kiote/pi-setup/tree/main/herdr/agent-folders

This folder contains modified copies of files from herdr-app:
https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app
License: Apache License 2.0. The full license text is in LICENSE in this folder
(the same text as https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app/blob/master/LICENSE).
The upstream repository has no NOTICE file.

The upstream files are at commit d5edc016feaca968ce5b6e9fa3cb53a6e93ddd75
(the files that herdr-app 0.1.12 installed in ~/.config/herdr-app):
- defaults/mods/agents/main.js
- defaults/mods/pane/main.js and its five .svg icons
- defaults/mods/tabs/main.js, mod.json and its four win-*.svg icons
- defaults/layouts/main.json

Changes:

mods/agent-folders/ (from the `agents` mod)
- The list shows agents in folders that the user makes. Each folder has a
  name, a color, optional rules and a folded state. The folders are in the
  shared state key "agentFolders".
- Group order: "Pinned", then each folder, then "Unsorted". The space groups
  and the status sections (Needs you, Done, Working, Idle) are removed.
- A manual folder choice is the terminal label "agentfolders.folder". The mod
  writes it with the program `hc label`. Without a label, the first folder
  with a matching rule gets the agent. Rules use the prefixes space:, cwd:,
  app:, title: and tab:, the wildcard * and ~ for the home folder.
- New: drag an agent to a folder, drag a folder header to move the folder,
  a right-click menu for agents and folders, and a dialog to make or edit a
  folder. The mod draws its own menus and dialog.
- A colored bar on each agent row shows its folder color. The tree lines of
  sub-agents and the left edge of the narrow rail use the same color.
- The sort popup is replaced by one button: inside folders, sort by status
  or keep the space order. A second button makes a new folder.
- A row always shows "space · detail". The rule that hides duplicate details
  is removed.
- Folded sub-agents show "+N" on the row. The fold chevron is removed.
  A click on the agent icon still folds and unfolds the sub-agents.
- The working icon is static (no `.spin`). This saves CPU on a machine
  without a GPU.
- New: on Windows, a dot on the taskbar button. It is orange when an agent
  is blocked, else green when an agent is done. The mod runs the program
  `hc-badge` (from herdr/taskbar-badge/ in pi-setup) only when the state
  changes.
- The migration of old pins (localStorage "pins") is removed.
- The text for an empty list is shorter. The header and row sizes are a
  little different.
- Most comments are removed or shorter.

mods/pane-labels/ (from the `pane` mod)
- The header shows the terminal label "pane.title" after the agent name.
  Set it with `hc label <terminal> pane.title=<title>`.
- The icon paths point to mods/pane-labels/. The header comment and the
  mod.json title are new.
- The working icon is static (no `.spin`).
- The five .svg icons are unchanged copies. herdr-app says that the glyphs
  in its shipped mods come from Lucide (ISC License, some icons MIT from
  Feather). See defaults/icons/LICENSES.md and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES in
  herdr-app. A copy of the Lucide license is in LICENSE-Lucide.txt.

mods/tabs-static/ (a clone of the `tabs` mod)
- The working icon is static (no `.spin`).
- The window button icon paths point to mods/tabs-static/.
- The mod.json has "cloned_from": {"name": "tabs", "version": "0.1.12"}.
- The four .svg icons are unchanged copies.

layouts/main-titles.json (a clone of the `main` layout)
- The agents block uses the mod "agent-folders" (was "agents").
- The pane header uses the mod "pane-labels" (was "pane").
- The tabs block uses the mod "tabs-static" (was "tabs").
- The clone has "cloned_from": {"name": "main", "version": "0.1.12"}.
